UNIX-CLUB(7)            42 UNIX Club Manual            UNIX-CLUB(7)

NAME
       unix-club - a student club for the UNIX philosophy,
       customization & ricing at 42 Lisboa

SYNOPSIS
       show up to a meetup
       ping rucosta or mju-ferr on the intra

DESCRIPTION
       The 42 UNIX Club (short brand: 42 UNIX) is a student club at
       42 Lisboa for people interested in UNIX operating systems and
       the UNIX philosophy, and in ricing and customizing Unix-like
       and Unix-certified systems: Linux, the BSDs and macOS.

       Its personality in three words: Minimal. Deliberate. Open.

       Minimal      small tools that do one thing well; lean
                    documents, short rules, lots of whitespace.
       Deliberate   every choice has a reason, and every rule
                    states its reason.
       Open         open source (free assets, libre fonts, docs in
                    a repo) and open to newcomers (plain language,
                    nothing gatekept).

PILLARS
       1. Educational
              Sharing and demystifying the UNIX philosophy, Linux
              fundamentals and general comfort in the terminal.

       2. Execution & showcasing
              Hands-on ricing, customization, dotfiles, and
              presenting members' own setups.

       3. Peer support
              A learning resource for students who hit UNIX and
              Linux details in their projects (Born2beroot and
              beyond). A resource to learn from, not a help desk,
              and never a source of project solutions.

       Across all three, the club values and encourages free and
       open-source solutions: software, hardware, and anything
       related.

ACTIVITIES
       o  Introductory sessions on ricing and customization.
       o  Theory sessions on the UNIX philosophy and Linux
          fundamentals.
       o  Hands-on sessions: terminal comfort, dotfiles, window
          managers.
       o  Aspirations: a themed setup contest, a shared dotfiles
          repo and setup gallery, a club web platform (an extra
          route, never the only one).

PROCEDURES
       The monthly meetup is the anchor and doubles as the club's
       internal meeting: ideas, showcases, attendance recorded.
       Topics and club-wide decisions are picked by poll: democracy,
       not sudo. Slack is the official channel; Discord hosts
       day-to-day chat, polls and showcases. Stickers and enamel
       pins are paid by the organizers or crowdfunded, never by the
       school. The club seeks no school budget.

MEMBERSHIP
       Lightweight: contact either contact person and show up to a
       meetup. Every new member is equal to every existing one; there
       is no inner circle.

CONTACTS
       rucosta     contact 1, primary
       mju-ferr    contact 2

FILES
       ~/unix_club/
              The club's intro session, one file per slide. Start with
              cat ~/unix_club/README.md or run sh ~/unix_club/intro.sh.

       ~/.shrc
              Your shell dotfile, with every line explained.

SEE ALSO
       sh(1), bc(1), the 42 Portugal student club rules, and
       r/unixporn for inspiration.

NOTES
       This system, UC.OS (UNIX CLUB dot OS), is the club's own
       operating system: a kernel and its programs, all WebAssembly,
       running in a browser tab.

BUGS
       0 known ways to exit vim. (It is <Esc>:wq.)

